# inc-j5yo: a Mage changes his spell loadout in the checklist, and the change
# takes effect only at the next full rest. Read by tools/check_mage_loadout.sh.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed1-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/mage-loadout-rest.keys 1
#
# THE CHARACTER. Varag, the frozen Orc Mage (tools/fixtures/chars/). The save
# is older than spell-flag revision 5, so loading migrates it: Shield and Magic
# Missile become class grants (locked), and Alarm, Burning Hands and Convulsion
# become the memorized arcane picks (level 1: 3 of 3 slots). He carries six
# spellbooks in his pack.
#
# THE ROUTE (each @dump label is one assertion screen in the check):
#   1. Wizard mode: descend to depth 2 (a rest is refused at depth 1) and
#      genocide everything (a rest is refused with a hostile in view).
#   2. d, L opens the checklist.                              open
#      DOWN*3 SPACE: mark Endure Cold with no slot free.      refused
#      UP SPACE: unmark Convulsion. DOWN SPACE: mark Endure
#      Cold.                                                  swapped
#      DOWN*10 SPACE: try to unmark Magic Missile (a grant).  locked
#      ENTER opens the "At your next full rest:" box (summary),
#      a second ENTER confirms. 'v' reads the message log.    msgs-enter
#      'm' opens the cast menu: Convulsion still castable,
#      Endure Cold not yet.                                   cast-before
#   3. Reopen, unmark Alarm, ESC: the change is discarded.    esc-pre, esc-post
#   4. Drop all six books (inventory item 16, six times).
#      Reopen: pending rows read "(no book)".                 rows-nobook
#   5. 'z' 'y' rests. The message names the three spells it
#      could not memorize; the cast menu has lost Convulsion
#      and gained nothing.                                    msgs-rest1, cast-nobook
#   6. Pick all six books up again ('g', choose, 's' stows),
#      rest again: Endure Cold, Alarm and Burning Hands are
#      memorized, Convulsion is gone.                         msgs-rest2, cast-after
#
# Keys that bite: lowercase 'v' is View Messages and 'z' is Rest (uppercase
# sets SHIFT and matches nothing, see src/KeyScript.cpp). The first ESC after
# ENTER only closes the sheet's message, so every exit uses
# @until "Things in View" ESC. Row counts (DOWN*3, DOWN*10) are positions in
# this frozen character's sorted level-1 list; LearnSpell sorts rows by name.

s                       # one real turn: this counts as a session
w y                     # wizard mode, confirm
@choose "Ascend / Descend Depth"
"2" ENTER
# The wizard descent keeps the player's x,y (Player::MoveDepth, safe=false), so a
# chasm square there makes the player fall; each fall asks for ENTER. Any number
# of falls is fine: the check needs only a level of depth 2 or more.
@while "You fall" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@until "HP:" ESC
# Stand on dry floor: the arrival square is the seed's (water would sink the
# dropped spellbooks). Change terrain type, cursor starts on the player.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
ENTER
e                       # the first "Floor" row (two rows share the name)
@until "HP:" ESC

d
L
@dump:open
DOWN*3
SPACE
@dump:refused
UP
SPACE
DOWN
SPACE
@dump:swapped
DOWN*10
SPACE
@dump:locked
ENTER
@dump:summary
ENTER
@until "Things in View" ESC
v
@dump:msgs-enter
ESC
m
@dump:cast-before
ESC

d
L
SPACE
@dump:esc-pre
ESC
L
@dump:esc-post
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC

i
1 6 d
1 6 d
1 6 d
1 6 d
1 6 d
1 6 d
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
d
L
@dump:rows-nobook
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC

z
y
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "[more]" SPACE
v
@dump:msgs-rest1
ESC
m
@dump:cast-nobook
ESC

g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC
g
@while "Pick up what?" a
s
ESC
@until "Things in View" ESC

z
y
@while "more --" SPACE
@while "[more]" SPACE
v
@dump:msgs-rest2
ESC
m
@dump:cast-after
ESC
@dump:end
